  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "Transform, then leap to an area that inflicts recurring HP-loss and bind.",
    "skill1": "Deal heavy single-target magic damage with smaller adjacent splash damage.",
    "skill2": "Temporarily increase self ATK and Haste.",
    "skill3": "Permanently increase Energy regeneration from attacks after transformation.",
    "skill4": "Distribute area missiles that eventually bind repeatedly hit targets.",
    "skill5": "Heal nearby allies over time after transformation and gain permanent ATK per ally."
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Yamato & Gabumon]] supports from the sidelines while the partner transforms after the first ultimate. The transformed form jumps into position to create a damaging area that binds enemies and applies repeated HP-loss. Repeated missiles add broad splash pressure and can lock down a focused target. Nearby allies receive a healing-over-time window after transformation. The duo is strongest after transformation and against grouped enemies, while early burst or spacing that limits missile splash reduces control and sustained area damage.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Yamato & Gabumon]] is weakest before the first ultimate transforms the pair; afterward, the jump zone applies repeated HP-loss and bind while missiles cover the field. Delay that first cast with [[Dunlingr]]'s ultimate lockout, then pressure the duo early with high-damage melee like [[Himmel]] or [[Zandrok]]. Spread key units so splash and the breath area cover fewer targets, then use cleanse or control immunity to limit the bind. Race the transformation with [[filter:energy-provider]] like [[Thador]] or [[Hugin]]."
}
